{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is contained in the interior of a larger circle with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b82496a03bd5d214987611c102f81a4dfa80ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1+A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />. If the radius of the larger circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, \nand if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210c593b3c73b127e245183f6e02fcdd9d0efb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 , A_2, A_1 + A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> is an arithmetic progression, then the radius of the smaller circle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82da662ce0c3da1fb11c5ec07e85399fa24f01f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{3}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"411\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>The area of the larger circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/13818fdf7d96915fd7f16b348df89c0a2b2e2012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 + A_2 = 9\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bcea518fdf6a3976b9a86f70a61c42f2ea452a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 , 9\\pi-A_1 , 9\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" /> are in an arithmetic progression. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793b93d3eb48ed61eae2691a936c26495da92871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\pi-(9\\pi-A_1) = 9\\pi-A_1-A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"249\" height=\"18\" />. This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1fc58bec843c3103c64b72b9949e6cd0da0ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3A_1 = 9\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e919d8674baa0cf41d2463b156bdead30dcf70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 = 3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />. The radius of the smaller circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/14986ba3208630b9431f7d34a7209192f1866fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"69\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/